_{The first step in recovery is admission to an addiction treatment center. An admission counselor will interview the patient to determine their history of addiction and discuss how it has affected their important relationships, their health, and their work or school performance. The counselor will also discuss detoxification or inpatient treatment with the patient to determine which option is best for the addict and their family.}
_{Inpatient or residential drug rehabs provide intensive, on-site therapeutic and counseling services. Patients live at the rehab and participate in various therapeutic programs, such as one-on-one and group counseling sessions, educational instruction, and 24-hour supervision. Patients may receive medication as part of an integrated treatment program to manage withdrawal symptoms or co-occurring medical or mental health issues.}
_{The United States' approach to substance abuse has shifted over the years from an almost entirely biologically-based view, which only focused on abstinence, to a more holistic view that incorporates treatment into problem and recovery. (28) Bio-models are based on the idea that addiction is entirely physical and sentimental, and opinions about addiction often emphasized the idea of treatment as simply talking to drug addicts, and offering the classic slogan "Just say no to drugs." However, some recent studies in the late 1990s and early 2000s showed that a more holistic approach was the most effective in treating addiction. (29) This approach often incorporates medications, psychotherapy, counseling, support groups, and social support into a comprehensive treatment plan. (30)}
